  "camera": {
    "_about": "The camera over the room picture (b1) and her close-up (art.faceShot): wide is a centre in the room picture's pixels and a zoom over the cover fit; face is a centre in the close-up's pixels and a zoom over its cover fit (inside its feathered edge). The moves: the push-in to her face (toFaceMs: the room grows, the close-up fades in over its last part), the turn down to the book (tiltMs: the close-up slides up as the pages come up under it, lined up, art.faceShot.pagesIn), the page turn, the way back out (the turn up to her face, then the pull back to the whole room: outMs). They always take their real time, also at test speed, so a filmstrip sees them. maxUpscale: never more screen px per picture px than this (ART-05) once a shot is still. No player character (Zafar, 19 Oct).",
